--- samtools view -T data/
data/genome.fa 
--- bwa mem -
-5 	for split alignment, take the alignment with the smallest query (not genomic) coordinate
-A 	score for a sequence match, which scales options -TdBOELU unless overridden
-B 	penalty for a mismatch
-C 	append FASTA/FASTQ comment to SAM output
-D 	drop chains shorter than FLOAT fraction of the longest overlapping chain
-E 	gap extension penalty; a gap of size k cost '{-O} + {-E}*k'
-H 	insert STR to header if it starts with @; or insert lines in FILE
-I 	specify the mean, standard deviation (10% of the mean if absent), max
-K 	process INT input bases in each batch regardless of nThreads (for reproducibility)
-L 	penalty for 5'- and 3'-end clipping
-M 	mark shorter split hits as secondary
-O 	gap open penalties for deletions and insertions
-P 	skip pairing; mate rescue performed unless -S also in use
-R 	read group header line such as '@RG\tID:foo\tSM:bar'
-S 	skip mate rescue
-T 	minimum score to output
-U 	penalty for an unpaired read pair
-V 	output the reference FASTA header in the XR tag
-W 	discard a chain if seeded bases shorter than INT
-Y 	use soft clipping for supplementary alignments
-a 	output all alignments for SE or unpaired PE
-c 	skip seeds with more than INT occurrences
-d 	off-diagonal X-dropoff
-h 	if there are <INT hits with score >80.00% of the max score, output all in XA [5,200] A
-j 	treat ALT contigs as part of the primary assembly
-k 	minimum seed length
-m 	perform at most INT rounds of mate rescues for each read
-o 	sam file to output results to
-p 	smart pairing (ignoring in2.fq)
-q 	don't modify mapQ of supplementary alignments
-r 	look for internal seeds inside a seed longer than {-k} * FLOAT
-t 	number of threads
-u 	output XB instead of XA; XB is XA with the alignment score and mapping quality added
-v 	verbosity level: 1=error, 2=warning, 3=message, 4+=debugging
-w 	band width for banded alignment
-x 	read type
-y 	seed occurrence for the 3rd round seeding
-z 	the fraction of the max score to use with -h
--- borg create --compression 
auto,	compress only data that lz4 finds compressible
lz4 	very high speed, very low compression (default)
lzma 	low speed, high compression (level 6)
lzma,	lzma with a level (0-9)
none 	no compression
obfuscate,	obfuscate the sizes of the compressed chunks
zlib 	medium speed, medium compression (level 6)
zlib,	zlib with a level (0-9)
zstd 	modern wide-range algorithm (level 3)
zstd,	zstd with a level (1-22)
